WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.000
You opened the file. You watched a case walk into a law firm at 8:47 at night and walk right back out.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:34.000
I'm Dario. I built SaveCases. This briefing is about the quiet version of that story—the phone may never even ring.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:54.000
It's 8:47 on a Tuesday night. An injured person does not have a lawyer and is not waiting until morning to find one.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Your firm might be sitting right there on the list. Better results. Better reviews. Years in the county.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Two results down, another firm looks reachable. The caller reaches them, tells the story, and books the morning consultation.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:57.000
There may be no missed call, no voicemail, no trace. There is no record anywhere that an opportunity disappeared.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:20.000
The better lawyer did not necessarily win. The reachable lawyer got the first conversation. That is the physics of after hours.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:42.000
You cannot audit this loss, and that is exactly what makes it expensive. There is no line item for cases that never called.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:03:03.000
It only takes one meaningful matter for the after-hours window to justify serious attention. The real count remains invisible.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:24.000
Here is what SaveCases is. It is after-hours intake designed for one job: advancing injury inquiries while the office is dark.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:47.000
A call comes in. The caller is answered and a structured intake begins: what happened, when, the injuries, treatment, and relevant facts.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:04:09.000
The caller is taken seriously at the exact moment other paths are asking them to try again tomorrow.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:31.000
The firm receives the captured facts, organized and ready for review. Designated situations can follow the firm's escalation protocol.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:53.000
You should test the experience for yourself. Use a difficult fact pattern. Interrupt it. Change details. See how the intake responds.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:05:15.000
The purpose of a controlled test is to observe the after-hours pattern on your own line, with your own callers and criteria.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:38.000
Every call is answered, each intake is documented, and your team can review the results. Spam and unrelated calls are separated out.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:06:00.000
The goal is not to replace legal judgment. It is to make sure a credible opportunity does not vanish before that judgment can occur.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:22.000
When coverage is active, the firm no longer disappears at the end of the business day. The after-hours caller has a real next step.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:48.490
Below this video is a button to open a private conversation about the test and whether it fits the firm.

